<!--
    The whole PiKit pixel wordmark, for in-app use wherever the app draws its logo.

    The path data is `ic_launcher_foreground`'s, character for character, moved so
    its bounding box starts at the origin: the launcher's copy sits on (26.7, 45.6)
    of the 108-unit adaptive-icon layer, and the group below subtracts exactly that.
    That is why this file has no re-cut geometry — the app's logo and the icon a
    reader taps are one drawing, so the tap and the screen it opens cannot read as
    two different marks.

    **The compact P is for the avatar and the shade only.** `ic_pi_mark.xml` is the
    first letter alone, which is what survives a 28–34dp circle and a 24dp status
    bar; at logo size the whole name is drawn instead, because a mark that is only a
    letter is not the app's icon. The launcher foreground, this file, the avatar and
    `ic_notification` are therefore four deliberate sizes of one drawing rather than
    four logos.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
